<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chełmno Land</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kulmerland, Culmerland, Ziemia chełmińska</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno">Chełmno</a> Land is a historical region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, around the town of Chełmno (Kulm). <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-masovia">Konrad I of Masovia</a> granted it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in the 1220s as a base for the conquest of the pagan Prussians, and it became the core of the order's state. It returned to Poland under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a> in 1466.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chelmno-land.jpg" alt="Chełmno Land" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sirleonidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grudzi%C4%85dz_view_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
